  ██║  ██║██║██║  ██║╚██████╔╝
  ╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═╝╚═╝  ╚═╝ ╚═════╝
  </pre>
</p>

**Hiro** is a Claude Code-grade terminal AI coding assistant with:
- 🤖 **Multi-provider support** — Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Groq, DeepSeek, Mistral, Ollama, and any OpenAI-compatible API
- 🔌 **MCP integration** — Connect BurpSuite, Nuclei, Metasploit, and any MCP server
- 🔒 **Cybersecurity tooling** — Built-in `/scan`, `/burp`, `/audit`, `/payload`, `/secrets`, `/sqli`, `/xss` commands
- ⚡ **Token-efficient** — No bloated pre-prompts. Zero mandatory system prompt.
- 🛠  **35+ slash commands** — Model switching, context management, file ops, and more
- 🎨 **Beautiful TUI** — Rich terminal output with syntax highlighting, themes, and streaming

---

## Installation

```bash
# Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/yourname/hiro
cd hiro

# Install with pip (editable mode)
pip install -e ".[all]"

# Or with specific providers only:
pip install -e ".[anthropic]"   # Anthropic only
pip install -e ".[openai]"      # OpenAI only
pip install -e "."              # Core only (httpx-based)
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Set your API key
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# Start Hiro
hiro

# Or with a specific model
hiro -m gpt-4o -k sk-...

# One-shot query
hiro "Explain this code: $(cat main.py)"

# Use local Ollama
hiro -m ollama/llama3.2

# List all available models
hiro --list-models
```

## Configuration

Copy the example config to get started:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/hiro
cp hiro.toml.example ~/.config/hiro/config.toml
```

Then edit `~/.config/hiro/config.toml` with your API keys and MCP servers.

## Slash Commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `/help` | Show all commands |
| `/model [name]` | Switch AI model |
| `/key <provider> <key>` | Set API key |
| `/temperature <val>` | Set temperature |
| `/provider url <p> <url>` | Set custom base URL |
| `/system [prompt]` | Set system prompt |
| `/context` | Show context info |
| `/compact [n]` | Compact conversation |
| `/reset` | Clear conversation |
| `/history [n]` | Show message history |
| `/tokens` | Show token usage |
| `/file <path>` | Add file to context |
| `/import <url>` | Import URL to context |
| `/diff [f1 f2]` | Show git/file diff |
| `/cd <path>` | Change directory |
| `/ls [path]` | List directory |
| `/run <cmd>` | Run shell command |
| `/shell` | Open interactive shell |
| `/mcp list` | List MCP servers |
| `/mcp tools` | List MCP tools |
| `/mcp connect <name>` | Connect MCP server |
| `/mcp call <tool> [args]` | Call MCP tool directly |
| `/mcp resources` | List MCP resources |
| `/mcp prompts` | List MCP prompts |
| `/scan <target>` | Security scan (nmap/nuclei) |
| `/burp <action>` | BurpSuite via MCP |
| `/audit <target>` | Full security audit |
| `/payload <type>` | Generate pentest payloads |
| `/sqli <url>` | SQL injection test |
| `/xss <url>` | XSS test |
| `/secrets [path]` | Scan for secrets |
| `/decode <str>` | Decode base64/JWT/hex |
| `/hash <str>` | Hash a string |
| `/save [name]` | Save session |
| `/load [name]` | Load session |
| `/config show` | Show config |
| `/theme [name]` | Change color theme |
| `/clear` | Clear screen |
| `/exit` | Exit Hiro |

## BurpSuite MCP Setup

1. Install the BurpSuite MCP extension
2. Configure in `~/.config/hiro/config.toml`:

```toml
[[mcp_servers]]
name = "burp"
command = ["node", "/path/to/burp-mcp-server/index.js"]
transport = "stdio"
enabled = true
tags = ["security", "burp"]
[mcp_servers.env]
BURP_API_KEY = "your-key"
BURP_URL = "http://localhost:1337"
```

3. Use from Hiro:
```
/burp tools              # List available BurpSuite tools
/burp scan https://...   # Active scan
/burp history            # View proxy history
```

## Multi-Provider Examples

```bash
# Anthropic Claude
hiro -m claude-opus-4-5

# OpenAI GPT-4o
hiro -m gpt-4o
export OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."

# Google Gemini
hiro -m gemini-2.5-pro
export GOOGLE_API_KEY="AIza..."

# Groq (fast inference)
hiro -m llama-3.3-70b-versatile
export GROQ_API_KEY="gsk_..."

# DeepSeek
hiro -m deepseek-chat
export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="sk-..."

# OpenRouter (any model)
hiro -m meta-llama/llama-3.2-90b --url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-or-..."

# Local Ollama
hiro -m ollama/qwen2.5-coder

# Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint
hiro -m my-model --url http://localhost:8080/v1
```

## Token Efficiency

Hiro is designed to minimize unnecessary token usage:
- **No mandatory system prompt** — The AI gets your question immediately
- **Smart context compaction** — Auto-compacts at 80% context usage
- **Token tracking** — See exact token counts per response
- **`/compact`** — Manually trim context when needed
- **`/tokens`** — View full session token breakdown

## Themes

```bash
/theme dark    # Default (dark with purple accents)
/theme hacker  # Matrix green terminal aesthetic
/theme nord    # Arctic blue-gray palette
/theme light   # Light mode
```

